Target Environment & Compatibility

    Requires ATS v1.60+ or v1.61.

    Modified master files: /unit/hookup/animated_gate.sii, /unit/hookup/animated_gate.dlc_*.sii, and /unit/hookup/parked_vehicle.sii and def/world/trigger_action.sii.

    Verified cross-compatibility for the ATS Base Map, all official State DLCs, ProMods Canada, and Reforma Map Combos.

Smart Gate Clearance & Distance Standards

    135.0m Extended Tail-Swing Clearance: Applied to Oregon heavy metal storage doors (metal_01) to prevent long trailer clipping.

    125.0m Universal High-Speed Approach: Applied to high-traffic entry points in Illinois (dlc_il), New Mexico (dlc_nm), and Texas (dlc_tx).

    25.0m Stop-and-Go & Weigh Stations: Applied to state border inspection scale houses, weigh stations, river locks, and floodgates—retaining stock engine mechanics and native 25m triggers to protect baseline weighing logic and prevent trigger breakage.

    20.0m Security & Guard Inspection: Applied to international borders, maritime ports, and mining facilities using a 90° orientation.

    17.0m Pneumatic & Short-Range: Applied to industrial yards across Kansas, Montana, Oklahoma, and Wyoming.

    Custom Asset Colliders: Explicit physical .pmc files assigned to custom assets including ag_nv_wstg and ag_suncrops.

Animated Gate Group Structure Index

    Groups 1 & 2: Standard toll booths and weigh station scale arms retaining stock engine mechanics paired with 25m guarded barriers.

    Group 3: Base Map and Western/Mountain expansions configured with 125.0m standard or 17.0m pneumatic triggers.

    Group 4: Directional rotary/swing gates and heavy access doors tuned between 125.0m and 135.0m.

    Groups 5 & 6: Midwest (dlc_il, dlc_mo, dlc_ia) and Southern DLC regional gate networks.

    Group 7: Dynamic movers and bridge gates running 25.0m ranges, 100° orientation, and /sound/world/gate_iron.soundref audio.

    Group 8: Secure industrial perimeters, refineries, mines, and ports utilizing a 20.0m range and 90° orientation.

    Group 9: Framework preparations establishing rules for upcoming state expansions like North Dakota, Indiana, and South Dakota.

Parked Fleet & Parking Density Architecture

    85 Integrated Categories: Fully expanded fleet rebalance handling all vehicle profiles with 100% vanilla traffic compliance, stripping all obsolete or modded vehicle strings.

    Namespace De-duplication: Base unit names in parked_vehicle.sii rewritten to prevent runtime parser collisions with base assets and major map mods.

    Deterministic Shift Ratios: Enforces dynamic probability multipliers (scaling up to 2.0 for overnight rest stops and rural clusters).

    Yard Trailer Rules: Configured with high daytime weights and optimized night weights, pairing with mandatory rear_align: true tags.

    Night Light Rules: Enforces forced_flare_low_beam: true and active warning flares (forced_flare_hooter: true) across emergency, enforcement, and night-shift fleet profiles.

    VRAM Optimization: Background variants use low_poly_only: true and always_visible: false. Recommended console setting: uset g_lod_factor_parked "1.1".
    
Weight Stations

	Weight stations went from 80% stop chance to 20% to be more realistic.

Bug Fixes & Stability Cleanups

    Parser Crash Resolution: Eliminated duplicate unit errors caused by legacy suv.always.parked.physics registrations and third-party truck mod clashes.

    Vanilla Traffic Enforcement: Scrubbed non-native vehicle definitions to ensure zero missing asset logs under ATS v1.60+ runtime environments.
